// Title: System Integrity Protection (SIP) Disabled
// Sigma ID: 3603f18a-ec15-43a1-9af2-d196c8a7fec6
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Joseliyo Sanchez, @Joseliyo_Jstnk
// Date: 2024-01-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1518.001
// Description: Detects the use of csrutil to disable the Configure System Integrity Protection (SIP). This
//   technique is used in post-exploit scenarios.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://ss64.com/osx/csrutil.html
//   - https://objective-see.org/blog/blog_0x6D.html
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/2017/10/20/osx-proton-supply-chain-attack-elmedia/
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/05a2adb266ec6c0ba9ed176d87d8530e71e845348c13caf9f60049760c312cd3/behavior
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_csrutil_disable.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/csrutil" and ProcessCommandLine contains "disable"
